  "starterCode": "import numpy as np\n\ndef ml_pca(X: list, k: int = 2) -> dict:\n    pass",
  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nThe implementation computes **PCA from Scratch** by following direct mathematical principles, leveraging vectorized operations to ensure both correctness and optimal runtime efficiency.\n\n### ⚡ Python Reference Implementation\n```python\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef ml_pca(X: list, k: int = 2) -> dict:\n    arr = np.array(X, dtype=float)\n    cen = arr - np.mean(arr, axis=0)\n    cov = (cen.T @ cen) / (arr.shape[0] - 1)\n    evals, evecs = np.linalg.eigh(cov)\n    idx = np.argsort(evals)[::-1][:k]\n    top_vecs = evecs[:, idx]\n    return {'projected': np.round(cen @ top_vecs, 4).tolist(), 'components': np.round(top_vecs.T, 4).tolist(), 'explained_variance': np.round(evals[idx], 4).tolist()}\n```\n\n### ⏱️ Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where $N$ represents the size of the primary input.\n- **Space Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ auxiliary memory for computing and storing output representations.",
